# REVEAL SMOKE: the dark smoke a demon gives off at the moment the light makes it solid (a lantern field, a
# searchlight cone, a staff light). One puff per demon, through ParticleSystem::emitPuff (GameUnitComponent::setSolid),
# which draws at most 12 puffs a frame: so `Rate` is 0 and `Burst` is the puff's particle count.
# IT MUST READ AT NIGHT, AND STAY DARK IN A BRIGHT FIELD: pure black unlit smoke is invisible at night, and a light
# grey lit smoke goes white in the field's light. So the colour is a DARK violet (about 10 % albedo), LIT - the
# field's gold light and the searchlight catch it without washing it out - with an emissive floor of a half: that
# share of its own colour shows with no light on it at all. Not additive: it stays smoke.
ParticleEffect RevealSmoke
	Emitter Smoke
		Texture Textures/Particles/smoke_puff.dds
		Rate 0
		Burst 7
		SpawnRadius 0.5
		Offset 0, 0.5, 0
		ConeAngle 70
		Speed 0.8 2.2
		Life 1.3 2.4
		Gravity -1.4
		Drag 1.3
		Turbulence 1.8 0.7 0.4
		Size 0.7 2.1
		SizeVariance 0.35
		ColorStart 0.10, 0.075, 0.13, 0.9
		ColorEnd 0.05, 0.04, 0.07, 0
		Additivity 0
		Lit true
		EmissiveFloor 0.5
		FadeIn 0.08
		FadeOutStart 0.4
		SoftFade 0.4
		Spin 1.0
